    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕōtĕrĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεωτερικός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>New, modern</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scriptor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Mamert. de Stat. Anim. 1, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕōtĕrĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>modern writers</i>, Aur. Vict. de Orig. Gent. Rom. <i>init.</i> —Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕōtĕrĭcē</span></b> ,
				<i>after a modern fashion</i>: dicere, Ascon. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Div. in Caecil. 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
